    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for ansible-collection-redhat-leapp.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 9.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "redhat.leapp Ansible collection that handles Rocky Linux upgrades.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* ansible-collection-redhat-leapp: ansible-collection-redhat-leapp: Information disclosure of PostgreSQL data via insecure backup permissions (CVE-2026-68563)\n\n* ansible-collection-redhat-leapp: ansible-collection-redhat-leapp: Information disclosure via Leapp report tampering (CVE-2026-68562)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
